WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
 You know the old
saying "Everything

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.660
happens for a reason"?

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.415
That reason is usually physics.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.420
I'm Bill Nye.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.640
You may know me as
the "Science Guy."

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.660
Yes!

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.760
I use science to solve
problems and make things.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.590
When you think
scientifically, that

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.380
enables you to attack
virtually any problem.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.470
I don't want everybody to
become a full-time scientist.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:31.840
The fashion consequences of that
alone would be very troubling.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.960
But we do want everybody to
have a fundamental knowledge

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.970
of science and an appreciation
of critical thinking.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.320
[LAUGHING SINISTERLY]

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.870
This class is a
shift in perspective.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.730
I'll show you some
ideas that I've come up

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.300
with over the last 40 years,
stuff I've never discussed

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.830
on any television show,
a way of thinking,

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:56.800
a way of accomplishing goals,
a way to not be fooled.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.760
It's very easy to think
something is a reliable source

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.200
when it might not be.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.230
Ask yourself, is
the claim specific?

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.420
Is there a simpler explanation?

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:11.570
And can it be
independently verified?

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.950
We've all felt fear.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.330
And fear comes
from the amygdala.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.870
Our brain gets hijacked--
affects your ability

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.040
to think logically.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.870
If you like to
worry about things,

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:22.410
you're living at a great time.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.530
And if you're like me,
you're very concerned

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:25.640
about climate change.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.750
There are more fires.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:27.890
There are more floods.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.600
The world's warmer than ever.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.880
But with our scientific
understanding,

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.180
we can take that fear and
turn it into excitement.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.980
We're going to talk
about the solutions

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:40.670
and how design will help us
all address big problems,

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.720
turning nerd ideas
into nerd action.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.550
And that, my friends,
is the essence

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.370
of science, the
joy of discovery.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:52.430
You learn more about yourself
and your relationship

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.690
to the world around you.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.490
We need big ideas.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.710
And those are going to
come from you and me.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:00.750
Just think what is possible
in the next few decades.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.210
It fills me with optimism
about the future.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:07.200
Let us think critically
to save the world.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.159
I'm Bill Nye, and
this is MasterClass.

